{"id": "sfmta-service-contracts-outlive-their-bids", "title": "Muni’s towing and paratransit contracts outgrew their bids: $290 million added", "seconds": 126.0, "voice": "elevenlabs:OtHu0lbpdNTqJVqaxDtR", "narrator": "Maven", "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "e4ccf4ed008be267", "words": 394, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["timeline[0]", "actors[2]"], "text": "Since 2004, one firm has towed San Francisco’s illegally parked cars:", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.28, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "TEGSCO, LLC", "kicker": "San Francisco AutoReturn", "sub": "towing contractor since 2004"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.45, 0.82, 1.63, 1.9, 2.19, 2.35, 2.71, 2.91, 3.56, 4.07, 4.37]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["timeline[0]", "actors[2]"], "text": "AutoReturn, now TEGSCO.", "t0": 5.28, "t1": 7.21, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "TEGSCO, LLC", "kicker": "San Francisco AutoReturn", "sub": "towing contractor since 2004"}, "wt": [0.04, 1.1, 1.33]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["timeline[1]", "actors[3]", "story[0]"], "text": "Since 2010, Transdev has run paratransit rides for people who cannot use buses.", "t0": 7.33, "t1": 11.51, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "Transdev Services, Inc.", "sub": "paratransit broker since 2010"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.24, 0.54, 0.96, 1.46, 1.57, 1.76, 2.36, 2.63, 2.78, 3.06, 3.17, 3.49, 3.66]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 11.63, "t1": 13.26, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in the Board’s own record. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.29, 0.37, 0.94, 1.11, 1.18]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "established[2]"], "text": "Both were bid in 2015, for ten years at most.", "t0": 13.38, "t1": 15.99, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Both bid in 2015", "sub": "for 10 years at most"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.36, 0.56, 0.65, 0.93, 1.56, 1.73, 1.89, 2.09, 2.17]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["amount", "story[2]"], "text": "How much have amendments added to the two since?", "t0": 16.11, "t1": 18.57, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Towing and paratransit", "kicker": "Amended again and again", "sub": "2016 to February 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.35, 0.5, 0.99, 1.23, 1.34, 1.44, 1.64]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "story[2]"], "text": "289,600,468 dollars, in ceilings, not spending.", "t0": 18.57, "t1": 22.37, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$289,600,468", "label": "added by amendment, towing and paratransit", "sub": "contract ceilings, not spending"}, "emph": ["289,600,468"], "wt": [0.04, 0.32, 0.47, 0.73, 1.18, 1.42, 1.67, 1.96, 2.34, 2.47, 3.15, 3.35]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[0]"], "text": "The 2015 towing request drew three bids; TEGSCO scored highest.", "t0": 22.99, "t1": 27.12, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "btow", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 28 January 2026", "text": "the incumbent provider since 2004, was the highest-scoring proposer out of three bids", "mark": "three bids"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.37, 0.77, 1.09, 1.52, 1.73, 1.96, 2.78, 3.32, 3.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]", "timeline[11]"], "text": "Approved in 2016 at 65.4 million dollars, it reached 158.8 million.", "t0": 27.24, "t1": 32.65, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["approved, March 2016", "$65.4 million"], "b": ["tenth amendment, February 2026", "$158.8 million"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["158.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.39, 0.49, 0.77, 1.28, 1.39, 1.94, 2.17, 2.38, 2.66, 3.12, 3.29, 3.59, 3.8, 4.07, 4.54, 4.8, 5.03]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "span", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]", "timeline[11]"], "text": "It now runs to June 2027, past the ten years the bid contemplated.", "t0": 32.77, "t1": 36.41, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2016-04-01", "to": "2027-06-30", "days": null, "fromLab": "towing contract begins", "toLab": "tenth amendment ends", "kicker": "beyond the initially contemplated 10-year term"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.31, 0.54, 0.67, 0.89, 1.11, 1.8, 2.09, 2.2, 2.44, 2.69, 2.79, 2.99]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "One amendment number was used twice, “due to administrative error”.", "t0": 36.53, "t1": 39.77, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Due to administrative error, this was also labeled as the First Amendment.", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, footnote 1"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.6, 0.88, 1.06, 1.28, 1.81, 2.14, 2.25, 2.88]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "notEstablished[1]", "innocent[4]"], "text": "By January 2026, the work had not gone back out to bid.", "t0": 39.89, "t1": 43.19, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "$829,400 a month", "kicker": "the management fee", "sub": "a new request was expected in early 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.65, 0.91, 1.64, 1.8, 2.0, 2.13, 2.29, 2.48, 2.69, 2.84, 2.94]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "The 2015 paratransit request drew a single respondent, Transdev.", "t0": 43.41, "t1": 47.27, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "bpar", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst · 11 February 2026", "text": "following a competitive bid process where Transdev was the sole respondent", "mark": "sole respondent"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.84, 1.43, 1.85, 2.1, 2.19, 2.46, 3.1]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]", "timeline[12]"], "text": "Approved in 2016 at 142.9 million dollars, it now stands at 339.1 million.", "t0": 47.39, "t1": 54.28, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "The paratransit contract ceiling", "rows": [["approved, June 2016", "$142,902,104"], ["sixth amendment, 2021", "$308,271,023"], ["tenth amendment, February 2026", "$339,102,572"]]}, "emph": ["339.1 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.45, 0.7, 1.13, 1.25, 1.43, 1.7, 2.28, 2.59, 2.87, 3.21, 3.98, 4.16, 4.35, 4.68, 4.82, 5.1, 5.39, 5.93, 6.26, 6.47]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[2]"], "text": "That makes 12 years in all, beyond the ten-year term the request advertised.", "t0": 54.4, "t1": 58.09, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "beyond the 10-year term advertised in the 2015 Request for Proposals", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, 11 February 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.43, 0.75, 1.01, 1.13, 1.52, 1.81, 1.91, 2.27, 2.5, 2.62, 2.99]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "With one bid, there was no market price to compare.", "t0": 58.21, "t1": 60.61, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "One bid", "sub": "no market price to compare"}, "emph": ["one bid"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.36, 0.92, 1.11, 1.22, 1.35, 1.62, 1.85, 1.94]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[3]", "timeline[5]"], "text": "The towing option began 1 April 2021; the Board approved it on 23 April, retroactively.", "t0": 60.83, "t1": 66.77, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Towing option, from 1 April 2021", "kicker": "Board File 21-0175", "sub": "approved 23 April 2021"}, "emph": ["retroactively"], "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.4, 0.68, 1.0, 1.19, 1.57, 1.86, 3.09, 3.24, 3.49, 3.83, 3.94, 4.06, 4.55, 5.12]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[3]"], "text": "The 2019 diesel contract is titled retroactive, but the old one was extended for Board review.", "t0": 66.89, "t1": 72.11, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Diesel contract, titled retroactive", "kicker": "Board File 19-0334", "sub": "old contract extended through May 2019"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.39, 0.75, 1.04, 1.52, 1.64, 2.01, 3.04, 3.22, 3.34, 3.54, 3.83, 4.02, 4.42, 4.56, 4.81]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "The files do not say why the towing option came late.", "t0": 72.23, "t1": 74.43, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "When a renewal reaches the Board after its term has begun, the Board votes on work already under way.", "kicker": "A renewal"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.47, 0.61, 0.78, 0.96, 1.12, 1.23, 1.5, 1.78, 1.98]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[5]"], "text": "The diesel contract shows the other path: one proposer in 2015, two in 2019.", "t0": 74.65, "t1": 79.6, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Bidders for the City’s renewable diesel", "rows": [["2015", "one responsive proposer"], ["2019", "two proposals"], ["2025", "four bids"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.42, 0.84, 1.06, 1.16, 1.37, 2.14, 2.35, 2.85, 2.95, 3.22, 3.93, 4.14, 4.22, 4.46]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[5]"], "text": "Golden Gate Petroleum won with a markup of $0.12 a gallon, against $0.40.", "t0": 79.72, "t1": 83.8, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Golden Gate Petroleum", "$0.12 a gallon"], "b": ["the other proposal", "$0.40"], "kicker": "markup over the published rack price, 2019", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.53, 1.1, 1.29, 1.45, 1.52, 1.89, 2.0, 2.29, 2.5, 2.55, 3.04, 3.37, 3.64]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "established[5]", "links[3]"], "text": "Four amendments took it from 45 million dollars to 108.6 million.", "t0": 83.92, "t1": 88.67, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$108.6 million", "label": "the 2019 diesel contract, after four amendments", "sub": "from $45 million; SFMTA made 77.4 percent of the purchases"}, "emph": ["108.6 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.73, 0.94, 1.04, 1.26, 1.83, 2.17, 2.94, 3.13, 3.31, 3.67, 3.84, 4.11, 4.38]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "established[5]", "timeline[10]"], "text": "SFMTA buys 77.4 percent of it. Rebid in 2025, it drew four bids.", "t0": 88.79, "t1": 94.14, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Rebid, 2025", "kicker": "four bids", "sub": "Golden Gate Petroleum lowest, up to $195.0 million"}, "emph": ["four bids"], "wt": [0.0, 0.73, 0.96, 1.56, 1.8, 2.01, 2.31, 2.4, 3.05, 3.45, 3.54, 3.82, 4.45, 4.54, 4.74, 4.95]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "SFMTA’s own fuel data covers one year, 2018 to 2019, with no prices.", "t0": 94.26, "t1": 99.24, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "MTA Fuel Usage", "kicker": "DataSF nz48-2k5q", "sub": "682 deliveries, July 2018 to June 2019, no prices"}, "wt": [0.0, 1.01, 1.23, 1.47, 1.71, 2.02, 2.2, 2.43, 2.73, 3.14, 3.22, 3.5, 4.08, 4.29, 4.43]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[7]", "innocent[5]"], "text": "SFMTA amends about as often as the City: 38 percent of money files, against 34.", "t0": 99.46, "t1": 104.76, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["SFMTA", "38%"], "b": ["citywide", "34%"], "kicker": "amendments among money files at the Board, 2014-2026", "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.82, 1.17, 1.38, 1.5, 1.81, 1.91, 2.03, 2.78, 3.26, 3.59, 3.7, 3.93, 4.35, 4.66]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[0]", "innocent[1]"], "text": "Federal law requires paratransit; State law caps towing fees at cost.", "t0": 104.88, "t1": 108.73, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "cityhall", "label": "Federal and State rules", "sub": "paratransit required since 1990; towing fees capped at cost"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 0.61, 1.01, 2.02, 2.32, 2.51, 2.78, 3.08, 3.28, 3.37]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["innocent[2]", "innocent[4]"], "text": "The pandemic delayed new bids, and new solicitations are planned.", "t0": 108.85, "t1": 111.79, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "New solicitations", "sub": "towing expected early 2026; paratransit Spring or Winter 2027"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.1, 0.55, 0.9, 1.06, 1.36, 1.51, 1.7, 2.39, 2.51]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[3]", "notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Nothing here says any contractor was paid more than the work cost.", "t0": 111.91, "t1": 114.82, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["Why the 2015 requests drew three bids and one", "Whether the costs reimbursed to Transdev were audited", "That any contractor was paid more than the work cost"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.52, 0.82, 1.01, 1.49, 1.6, 1.81, 1.96, 2.1, 2.2, 2.43]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The 2015 request files, and why others did not bid.", "t0": 114.94, "t1": 119.05, "shot": "b27", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The 2015 towing request file: plan holders, proposals and scores"}, {"who": "", "what": "The 2015 paratransit request file: why Transdev was the only respondent"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.37, 0.69, 1.2, 1.35, 1.63, 1.99, 2.35, 2.78, 2.91, 3.12, 3.45, 3.62, 3.8]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "defense[0]"], "text": "Every increase went to the Board, and its analyst recommended approving both.", "t0": 119.17, "t1": 123.01, "shot": "b28", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.66, 0.85, 0.94, 1.04, 1.74, 1.93, 2.08, 2.48, 3.05, 3.45]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 123.13, "t1": 125.1, "shot": "b29", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.35, 0.45, 0.52, 1.06, 1.26, 1.35]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Two contracts", "lead1": "Lead 1 · towing", "lead2": "Lead 2 · one bidder", "lead3": "Lead 3 · approved after the start", "lead4": "Lead 4 · diesel, rebid", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "map", "hook": "person"}